# issue: none
# notes: a three-way branch merge whose delta exceeds one write chunk (8192 rows) appends its second chunk to the merge scratch dataset through `append_or_create_batch`, the one scratch append that commits through the engine's commit constructor; the merged graph holds every row of both sides

--- runner
timeout_ms: 10000
environments:
  - target: omnigraph-engine-dst
    storage: in-memory-object-store
    seeds: [0]

--- schema
node Person {
    name: String @key
    v: I64
}

--- seed
{"type":"Person","data":{"name":"alice","v":0}}

--- mutate
branch create work

--- expect ok

--- load generate: v1 seed: 7 mode: append branch: work
tables:
  - kind: node
    name: Person
    rows: 9000
    commits: 3
    columns:
      name: {kind: key, prefix: person-, width: 5}
      v: {kind: ordinal, start: 0, step: 1}

--- expect ok

--- mutate
query add_bob() { insert Person { name: "bob", v: 1 } }

--- expect affected: nodes=1 edges=0

--- mutate
branch merge work

--- expect outcome: merged

--- query
query people() { match { $p: Person } return { count($p) as n } }

--- expect unordered
{"n": 9002}

--- expect shape
n: I64
